POLICY_VERSION 0.1.0

NAME Versioning and Release Cadence Policy

STATUS APPROVED

OWNER President Cley Duarte

DATE 2026-07-27

SCOPE PACE

SCHEME

Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 on the engine line (PACE_VERSION). While
pre-1.0: MINOR (0.x.0) for new user-facing features, PATCH (0.x.y) for
fixes and internal changes. The Instance Contract has its own independent
line (SCHEMA_VERSION); this policy governs the engine.

CADENCE

BATCH by default. Accumulate related work on main and cut a release when
there is a meaningful bundle of value, OR when a real user is blocked and
needs a fix now. Do NOT publish a new version per feature by default.
Every PyPI version is permanent and cannot be reused - treat each release
as a deliberate event, not a checkpoint.

RATIONALE

Four releases in one afternoon (0.2.0, 0.3.0, 0.3.1, 0.4.0) shipped real
value under a live feedback loop, which justified the speed then. But as a
default, high release frequency inflates the version number, clutters a
permanent history, and reads as instability to prospective buyers. Fewer,
larger, deliberate releases read as maturity.

ROAD_TO_1_0

1.0.0 is a stability COMMITMENT, not a feature count: it means the
Instance Contract and the CLI surface are stable enough that PACE promises
not to break them without a major bump. Candidate triggers: the
reality-comprehension / Governor milestone, or an explicit Presidential
decision that PACE is production-stable. Staying in 0.x is the honest
signal that the shape is still moving - that is a feature, not a defect.

END
